lowing compounds shows geometrical isomerism?&nbsp;"}, "options": [{"id": "d7df39", "text": "2-methylpent-2-ene", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f512ee0e063d9269561"}, {"id": "9ddb81", "text": "4-methylpent-2-ene", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f512ee0e063d9269562"}, {"id": "655b09", "text": "4-methylpent-1-ene", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f512ee0e063d9269563"}, {"id": "355f1d", "text": "2-methylpent-1-ene", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f512ee0e063d9269564"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f512ee0e063d9269565", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["617aa9f6ef3fe65ad8e8445b"], "concepts": ["617aa9f6ef3fe65ad8e8441b"], "question": {"text": "In Carius tube, an organic compound &#39; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math> &#39; is treated with sodium peroxide to form a mineral acid &#39; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></math> &#39;. The solution of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BaCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is added to &#39; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></math> &#39; to form a precipitate &#39; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi></math> &#39;. &#39; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi></math> &#39; is used for the quantitative estimation of an extra element. &#39; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math> &#39; could be"}, "options": [{"id": "859704", "text": "Cytosine", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f512ee0e063d9269566"}, {"id": "bce9dc", "text": "A nucleotide", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f512ee0e063d9269567"}, {"id": "40c91a", "text": "Methionine&nbsp;", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f512ee0e063d9269568"}, {"id": "e46476", "text": "Chloroxylenol", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f512ee0e063d9269569"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f512ee0e063d926956a", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["60e567ac499d1e49588f95ef"], "concepts": ["61f95ca5f4072e13fa37028a"], "question": {"text": "Given below are two statements:\nStatement I: In Lassaigne's test, the covalent organic molecules are transformed into ionic compounds.\nStatement II: The sodium fusion extract of an organic compound having N and S gives prussian blue colour with $\\mathrm{FeSO}_4$ and $\\mathrm{Na}_4\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{CN})_6\\right]$\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below."}, "options": [{"id": "62a8a3", "text": "Statement I is true but Statement II is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f512ee0e063d926956b"}, {"id": "15085b", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f512ee0e063d926956c"}, {"id": "e0a406", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f512ee0e063d926956d"}, {"id": "889d93", "text": "Statement I is false but Statement II is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f512ee0e063d926956e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f512ee0e063d926956f", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["60e5678e499d1e49588f927d"], "concepts": ["60e567c3499d1e49588f9946"], "question": {"text": "<p>Given below are two statement one is labeled as Assertion (A) and the other is labeled as Reason (R).</p><p>Assertion (A): <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>CH</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mi>Cl</mi></math> is an example of allyl halide<br/>Reason (R): Allyl halides are the compounds in which the halogen atom is attached to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> hybridised carbon atom.</p><p>In the light of the two above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "7872e2", "text": "(A) is true but (R) is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f512ee0e063d9269570"}, {"id": "237a3f", "text": "Both (A) and (R) are true but (R) is not the correct explanation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f512ee0e063d9269571"}, {"id": "bbf311", "text": "(A) is false but (R) is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f512ee0e063d9269572"}, {"id": "8b4492", "text": "Both (A) and (R) are true and (R) is the correct explanation of (A)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f512ee0e063d9269573"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f512ee0e063d9269574", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5676"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5654"], "question": {"text": "<p>Arrange the following amines in the decreasing order of basicity.<br /><br /><img height=\"138\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F944c506b-5df3-4aca-8875-a1c5a03b5726-image.png?alt=media\" width=\"214\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "cb5f70", "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f512ee0e063d9269575"}, {"id": "e4b3bb", "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f512ee0e063d9269576"}, {"id": "b3ef54", "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"no